  },
  "text": {
   "approach": "Drive Mt. Baker Highway (SR 542) to Hannegan Pass Road (FS 32); at 1.3 miles bear left onto Ruth Creek Road and continue to a pullout near milepost 3, just past a creek flowing over a concrete weir (about 2,950 ft), well short of the road's end at Hannegan Campground. From the pullout, cross Ruth Creek (a log crossing has been used) and bushwhack roughly 45 minutes through slide alder and devil's club to the base of the Wall Street couloir.",
   "approach_logistics": "{\"trailhead\":\"Ruth Creek Road pullout near milepost 3 (FS 32)\",\"trailheadDirection\":\"From a pullout near milepost 3 on Ruth Creek Road, just past a creek flowing over a concrete weir (~2,950 ft), off Hannegan Pass Road (FS 32) from the Mt. Baker Highway\"}",
   "road": "{\"name\":\"Hannegan Pass Road (FS 32) / Ruth Creek Road\",\"status\":\"Gravel Forest Service road to Hannegan Campground/trailhead\",\"driveNote\":\"From Mt. Baker Hwy (SR 542) ~12.5 mi east of Glacier, turn onto Hannegan Pass Rd (FS 32); at 1.3 mi bear left onto Ruth Creek Rd and continue to a roadside pullout near milepost 3, just past a creek flowing over a concrete weir, across Ruth Creek from the Wall Street couloir; do not drive on to the road's end at Hannegan Campground.\",\"seasonalGate\":\"Snow-closed in winter/spring; check Mt. Baker-Snoqualmie NF alerts for opening date\"}",
   "overview": "The classic north-side line: a steep snow gully ('Wall Street') gains the Northwest Glacier, which is crossed to a 6,500-ft saddle west of the summit, followed by a Class 2-3 scramble up the exposed southeast ridge to the top.",
   "description": null,
   "descent": "Reverse the southeast-ridge scramble to the 6,500-ft saddle, re-cross the Northwest Glacier, and plunge-step down the roughly 1,500-ft Wall Street couloir back to the bushwhack and Ruth Creek crossing."
  },
